  "body": "[`<button>`'s rendering](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#the-button-element-2) is currently defined in the [\"Bindings\"](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#bindings) section as opposed to either the [\"Replaced elements\"](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#replaced-elements) or [\"Non-replaced elements\"](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#non-replaced-elements) sections. I couldn't find anything else in the spec that clarifies this either.\nIs the `<button>` element a replaced element, or a non-replaced element? Or does/can its replaced-ness vary by circumstance? (If yes to the latter, please spell out the various circumstances.)\n[Firefox treats it as a replaced element](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1060131#c5); I presume other browsers don't, otherwise we'd be seeing the referenced bug in other browsers too.\n",
